1
00:00:01,168 --> 00:00:02,628
Great.

2
00:00:02,628 --> 00:00:04,546
Great. Just give me a sec
to change film.

3
00:00:04,546 --> 00:00:06,715
I know I'm not
supposed to know

4
00:00:06,715 --> 00:00:07,758
but I do.

5
00:00:07,758 --> 00:00:09,593
I'm so excited
for you.

6
00:00:09,593 --> 00:00:10,803
What's going on?

7
00:00:10,803 --> 00:00:13,931
Monica's pregnant!

8
00:00:13,931 --> 00:00:15,390
Oh, my God.

9
00:00:15,390 --> 00:00:17,184
Is that why you guys
had to get married?

10
00:00:17,184 --> 00:00:19,520
Guys, I'm not pregnant.

11
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:20,729
Oh. Slow swimmers?

12
00:00:23,774 --> 00:00:25,066
What?
What do you mean?

13
00:00:25,066 --> 00:00:26,568
You're not pregnant?

14
00:00:26,568 --> 00:00:28,445
You didn't tell anybody
I was, did you?

15
00:00:28,445 --> 00:00:32,240
No. I'll be right back.

16
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:34,326
Now, why don't
we get a shot

17
00:00:34,326 --> 00:00:35,953
of just Monica
and the bloody soldier?

18
00:00:35,953 --> 00:00:38,998
About that, Joey,
you have to change
before the party.

19
00:00:38,998 --> 00:00:40,916
I can't. I don't have
any other clothes here.

20
00:00:40,916 --> 00:00:42,584
Find some, please?

21
00:00:42,584 --> 00:00:45,921
Anything that doesn't say,
"I died tragically in France."

22
00:00:45,921 --> 00:00:47,214
Then why don't
we see the bride

23
00:00:47,214 --> 00:00:48,632
and the groom
and the bridesmaids?

24
00:00:48,632 --> 00:00:50,425
Okay.

25
00:00:51,969 --> 00:00:53,637
Hey, Mon, why'd
you tell the guys

26
00:00:53,637 --> 00:00:55,014
that you weren't pregnant?

27
00:00:55,014 --> 00:00:56,139
Because I'm not.

28
00:00:56,139 --> 00:00:58,099
We found your test
in the trash.

29
00:00:58,099 --> 00:00:59,643
If you're not pregnant...

30
00:01:04,189 --> 00:01:07,609
...it's because I am.

31
00:01:07,609 --> 00:01:08,819
What are you
talking about?

32
00:01:08,819 --> 00:01:10,070
What are you
talking about?

33
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:12,072
Yes, I am...

34
00:01:12,072 --> 00:01:14,825
I am with child.

35
00:01:14,825 --> 00:01:16,368
And I didn't want
to say anything

36
00:01:16,368 --> 00:01:17,619
because it's your day.

37
00:01:17,619 --> 00:01:19,246
I didn't want
to steal your thunder.

38
00:01:19,246 --> 00:01:20,539
Wait a minute.

39
00:01:20,539 --> 00:01:21,749
So you told people
I was pregnant?

40
00:01:21,749 --> 00:01:23,792
Does this look like
a conversation

41
00:01:23,792 --> 00:01:25,044
I want to remember?

42
00:01:25,044 --> 00:01:26,628
Who's the father?

43
00:01:26,628 --> 00:01:27,629
Yeah.

44
00:01:27,629 --> 00:01:29,673
I can't say.

45
00:01:29,673 --> 00:01:31,759
Why?
Why not?

46
00:01:31,759 --> 00:01:35,763
I can't say because he's famous.

47
00:01:35,763 --> 00:01:38,181
Oh, my God.
Who is it?

48
00:01:39,725 --> 00:01:40,809
Phoebe, come on.

49
00:01:40,809 --> 00:01:42,143
You have to tell us.

50
00:01:42,143 --> 00:01:43,144
Okay, okay.

51
00:01:43,144 --> 00:01:46,815
It's James Brolin.

52
00:01:46,815 --> 00:01:49,860
James Brolin is the father
of my baby.

53
00:01:49,860 --> 00:01:53,280
As in Barbra Streisand's
husband James Brolin?

54
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:57,659
What? Well, he never said that
to me.

55
00:02:04,374 --> 00:02:09,463
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

56
00:02:09,463 --> 00:02:12,007
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

57
00:02:12,007 --> 00:02:14,175
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

58
00:02:14,175 --> 00:02:19,056
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

59
00:02:19,056 --> 00:02:21,308
♪ When it hasn't been your day ♪

60
00:02:21,308 --> 00:02:24,603
♪ Your week, your month,
or even your year ♪

61
00:02:24,603 --> 00:02:27,940
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

62
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:33,904
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me too. ♪

63
00:02:36,197 --> 00:02:37,699
Monica, if you
could step away

64
00:02:37,699 --> 00:02:39,242
we'll get Chandler
and the bridesmaids.

65
00:02:39,242 --> 00:02:40,619
How about just
the bridesmaids?

66
00:02:40,619 --> 00:02:41,996
You know,
I am the groom.

67
00:02:41,996 --> 00:02:44,331
I was told it was
kind of a big deal.

68
00:02:44,331 --> 00:02:46,000
It is.

69
00:02:48,043 --> 00:02:49,168
Oh, my God.

70
00:02:49,168 --> 00:02:50,211
Thank you for
doing that.

71
00:02:50,211 --> 00:02:51,338
I just can't deal

72
00:02:51,338 --> 00:02:52,714
with this stress
quite yet.

73
00:02:52,714 --> 00:02:54,675
So instead you told me
Monica was pregnant?

74
00:02:54,675 --> 00:02:56,010
You said that she was.

75
00:02:56,010 --> 00:02:57,011
I just didn't
disagree with you.

76
00:02:57,011 --> 00:02:58,512
Sneaky.

77
00:02:58,512 --> 00:02:59,680
Yeah.

78
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:02,516
Smile, ladies.

79
00:03:02,516 --> 00:03:04,893
Oh, by the way,
James Brolin?

80
00:03:04,893 --> 00:03:06,020
Oh, I know.

81
00:03:06,020 --> 00:03:07,896
I could only think
of two names.

82
00:03:07,896 --> 00:03:09,982
Him and Ed Begley, Jr.
and then...

83
00:03:09,982 --> 00:03:13,610
I remembered
he's gay, so...

84
00:03:13,610 --> 00:03:16,279
Ed Begley, Jr.
is not gay.

85
00:03:16,279 --> 00:03:17,823
Really?

86
00:03:27,457 --> 00:03:29,459
Thank you very much.

87
00:03:29,459 --> 00:03:31,712
Ladies and gentlemen,
it gives me great pleasure

88
00:03:31,712 --> 00:03:33,797
to introduce to you
for the very first time

89
00:03:33,797 --> 00:03:36,341
Mr. and Mrs. Chandler Bing.

90
00:03:42,221 --> 00:03:43,598
Listen, before we go
out there

91
00:03:43,598 --> 00:03:44,683
I got a present
for you.

92
00:03:44,683 --> 00:03:45,809
Honey, I'm not going

93
00:03:45,809 --> 00:03:46,935
to put my hand
in your pocket.

94
00:03:46,935 --> 00:03:48,103
No.
No?

95
00:03:48,103 --> 00:03:49,479
I've been taking
dancing lessons.

96
00:03:49,479 --> 00:03:50,480
What?

97
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:52,273
Yeah, for the last
six weeks.

98
00:03:52,273 --> 00:03:55,360
I wanted this to be a moment
you would never forget.

99
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:57,154
That is so sweet.

100
00:03:57,154 --> 00:03:58,613
So, would you care
to join me

101
00:03:58,613 --> 00:04:00,699
in our first dance
as husband and wife?

102
00:04:00,699 --> 00:04:02,076
Yes.
Okay.

103
00:04:05,746 --> 00:04:07,789
What's the matter?

104
00:04:07,789 --> 00:04:09,166
It's these new shoes.

105
00:04:09,166 --> 00:04:10,584
They're all slippery.

106
00:04:10,584 --> 00:04:11,835
Are you going to be
able to do this?

107
00:04:11,835 --> 00:04:14,295
Not well.

108
00:04:20,219 --> 00:04:21,762
Well, the good news is

109
00:04:21,762 --> 00:04:23,805
I don't think
anyone's looking at us.

110
00:04:23,805 --> 00:04:28,393
So, you ready
to talk about it?

111
00:04:28,393 --> 00:04:31,105
No.

112
00:04:31,105 --> 00:04:34,149
Now?

113
00:04:34,149 --> 00:04:36,151
No.

114
00:04:36,151 --> 00:04:37,527
Okay, we'll talk
about something else, then.

115
00:04:37,527 --> 00:04:38,570
Okay.

116
00:04:38,570 --> 00:04:39,571
Who's the father?

117
00:04:39,571 --> 00:04:41,115
Oh!

118
00:04:41,115 --> 00:04:42,199
Look, honey, I haven't
told him yet

119
00:04:42,199 --> 00:04:43,700
so until I do

120
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:46,245
I don't think I should
tell anybody else.

121
00:04:46,245 --> 00:04:47,996
Yeah. That's fine.
That's fair.

122
00:04:47,996 --> 00:04:49,039
Thank you.

123
00:04:49,039 --> 00:04:50,207
Is it Tag?

124
00:04:50,207 --> 00:04:52,084
Oh! Phoebe!

125
00:04:52,084 --> 00:04:53,252
Okay, I'm sorry.
I'll stop.

126
00:04:53,252 --> 00:04:54,544
Okay.

127
00:04:54,544 --> 00:04:55,879
Is it Ross?
It's Ross, isn't it?

128
00:04:55,879 --> 00:04:57,589
Oh, my God!
It's Joey!

129
00:04:57,589 --> 00:04:58,715
Honey, stop it, okay?

130
00:04:58,715 --> 00:04:59,716
I am not going
to tell you

131
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:00,926
until I tell him.

132
00:05:00,926 --> 00:05:04,679
Aha! At least we know
it's a him.

133
00:05:09,851 --> 00:05:11,895
Oh, sweet Lord.

134
00:05:11,895 --> 00:05:12,896
I'm sorry, okay?

135
00:05:12,896 --> 00:05:14,273
I went down
to the gift shop

136
00:05:14,273 --> 00:05:16,108
and it was either this
or a bathrobe.

137
00:05:16,108 --> 00:05:17,484
Look, what's
more important:

138
00:05:17,484 --> 00:05:18,735
the way I'm dressed

139
00:05:18,735 --> 00:05:20,528
or me being with you
on your special day?

140
00:05:20,528 --> 00:05:21,780
Honey, I'm not going

141
00:05:21,780 --> 00:05:22,990
to even pretend
I was listening.

142
00:05:22,990 --> 00:05:23,991
Hey, hey.

143
00:05:29,079 --> 00:05:31,832
Hi.

144
00:05:31,832 --> 00:05:33,834
I'm Ross.
I don't believe we met.

145
00:05:33,834 --> 00:05:35,543
I'm Monica's older brother.

146
00:05:35,543 --> 00:05:37,963
Oh, hi. I'm Mona
from her restaurant.

147
00:05:37,963 --> 00:05:39,798
Oh.

148
00:05:39,798 --> 00:05:42,843
Hello, Mona
from her restaurant.

149
00:05:47,139 --> 00:05:49,891
Mona, what a beautiful name.

150
00:05:49,891 --> 00:05:51,143
You think so?

151
00:05:51,143 --> 00:05:52,811
I always kind of hated it.

152
00:05:52,811 --> 00:05:54,229
Aw, come on. Mona Lisa?

153
00:05:54,229 --> 00:05:55,272
Uh-huh.

154
00:05:55,272 --> 00:05:59,651
Mona... Kleckklecken.

155
00:05:59,651 --> 00:06:03,864
The famous botanist, huh?

156
00:06:03,864 --> 00:06:05,157
Oh, no, she's...

157
00:06:05,157 --> 00:06:07,408
Well, she's
dead now, but...

158
00:06:07,408 --> 00:06:10,704
Supposedly she was
once quite the hottie

159
00:06:10,704 --> 00:06:12,331
of the plant world.

160
00:06:12,331 --> 00:06:13,707
Really?

161
00:06:13,707 --> 00:06:15,125
Well, see, I never knew
about her.

162
00:06:15,125 --> 00:06:18,628
Linda Kleckklecken.

163
00:06:22,132 --> 00:06:24,467
So what.. what table
are you at?

164
00:06:24,467 --> 00:06:27,762
Oh, me, too.

165
00:06:27,762 --> 00:06:30,891
Good. Now there'll be someone
there who likes my name.

166
00:06:30,891 --> 00:06:32,642
Yes, there will.

167
00:06:39,274 --> 00:06:41,360
Oh, guess what, Molly Gilbert.

168
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:44,029
You've just been bumped up
to table one

169
00:06:44,029 --> 00:06:46,447
and if it's all right
with you

170
00:06:46,447 --> 00:06:49,826
I'm going to take your place
at table six.

171
00:06:49,826 --> 00:06:51,786
Martin Kleckklecken.

172
00:06:53,538 --> 00:06:54,831
That's better.

173
00:06:54,831 --> 00:06:56,541
Now bend you arms
a little bit.

174
00:06:56,541 --> 00:06:57,625
There you go. Okay.

175
00:06:57,625 --> 00:06:58,835
Look straight ahead.

176
00:06:58,835 --> 00:07:00,295
Now, this time
I want you

177
00:07:00,295 --> 00:07:02,047
to really put
your ass into it.

178
00:07:04,007 --> 00:07:05,675
Yeah.

179
00:07:05,675 --> 00:07:08,595
Chandler, darling, look,
my date has finally arrived.

180
00:07:08,595 --> 00:07:10,889
I'd like you to meet
Dennis Phillips.

181
00:07:10,889 --> 00:07:12,224
Congratulations.

182
00:07:12,224 --> 00:07:13,516
Thank you.

183
00:07:13,516 --> 00:07:15,560
Yes, Dennis, is
a dear old friend

184
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:17,062
and a fantastic lover.

185
00:07:17,062 --> 00:07:18,355
Bravo, Dennis.

186
00:07:18,355 --> 00:07:21,275
Thanks for pleasing
my mother so.

187
00:07:21,275 --> 00:07:23,735
Oh, I'm so sorry
I missed the ceremony.

188
00:07:23,735 --> 00:07:25,404
I was stuck at auditions.

189
00:07:25,404 --> 00:07:28,615
Oh, yes. Dennis is directing
a new Broadway show.

190
00:07:28,615 --> 00:07:31,118
I don't believe we've met.
Joey Tribbiani.

191
00:07:31,118 --> 00:07:32,577
Dennis Philipps.

192
00:07:32,577 --> 00:07:34,162
Oh, wow, I've admired
your work for years.

193
00:07:34,162 --> 00:07:35,914
You've done some
really amazing stuff.

194
00:07:35,914 --> 00:07:36,957
Oh, thank you.

195
00:07:36,957 --> 00:07:38,208
Well, if you'll
excuse me

196
00:07:38,208 --> 00:07:39,459
I'm going to go
get myself a drink.

197
00:07:39,459 --> 00:07:40,627
I'll be back
in a moment.

198
00:07:40,627 --> 00:07:42,087
Wow, Dennis Phillips.

199
00:07:42,087 --> 00:07:44,714
That's great.
How did you guys meet?

200
00:07:44,714 --> 00:07:46,633
Well, you know,
it's a funny story.

201
00:07:46,633 --> 00:07:47,926
Funny ha-ha
or funny...

202
00:07:47,926 --> 00:07:49,010
( imitates gunshot )

203
00:07:49,010 --> 00:07:50,345
Uh-oh!

204
00:07:57,894 --> 00:07:59,396
Thank you.
Thank you very much.

205
00:07:59,396 --> 00:08:01,273
Now if everyone will please
take your seats

206
00:08:01,273 --> 00:08:02,274
dinner will be served.

207
00:08:12,409 --> 00:08:17,247
Hey, I thought you
were at table six.

208
00:08:17,247 --> 00:08:19,374
Uh, no, nine.

209
00:08:19,374 --> 00:08:21,918
Oh, see

210
00:08:21,918 --> 00:08:24,212
before when you
showed it to me

211
00:08:24,212 --> 00:08:26,089
you held it
that way, which...

212
00:08:26,089 --> 00:08:28,133
( chuckles )

213
00:08:28,133 --> 00:08:30,260
...which was misleading.

214
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:33,638
Well...

215
00:08:40,854 --> 00:08:42,314
Hello.

216
00:08:48,653 --> 00:08:49,654
Hey, Chandler.

217
00:08:49,654 --> 00:08:50,697
Hey.

218
00:08:50,697 --> 00:08:51,948
Will you see
if your mom

219
00:08:51,948 --> 00:08:53,283
will give my resume
to Dennis Phillips?

220
00:08:53,283 --> 00:08:54,993
'Cause if I could get
in a Broadway show

221
00:08:54,993 --> 00:08:58,246
then I would have done it all:
film, television and theater.

222
00:08:58,246 --> 00:08:59,914
The only thing left
would be radio

223
00:08:59,914 --> 00:09:01,540
and that's just
for ugly people.

224
00:09:01,540 --> 00:09:04,085
What size shoes
do you wear?

225
00:09:04,085 --> 00:09:06,338
Uh, 11... 11 1/2.

226
00:09:06,338 --> 00:09:08,631
Great, because my shoes are
giving me a little problem.

227
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:10,467
Could I borrow the boots
from your costume?

228
00:09:10,467 --> 00:09:11,718
I don't even really know

229
00:09:11,718 --> 00:09:13,303
where I left those.
Huh. Sorry.

230
00:09:15,013 --> 00:09:17,224
Those aren't 11 1/2.

231
00:09:17,224 --> 00:09:18,766
Okay, fine. I'm a 7.

232
00:09:18,766 --> 00:09:21,395
All right? I have
surprisingly small feet.

233
00:09:21,395 --> 00:09:24,105
But the rest of me is good.
I'll show you.

234
00:09:26,441 --> 00:09:28,902
Can you believe
Phoebe got pregnant?

235
00:09:28,902 --> 00:09:30,320
Oh, you know what, honey?

236
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:31,488
Let's not talk
about that right now.

237
00:09:31,488 --> 00:09:32,947
This is so huge!

238
00:09:32,947 --> 00:09:35,574
Sure, but come on,
as big as your wedding?

239
00:09:35,574 --> 00:09:37,285
Of course not.
Nothing is.

240
00:09:37,285 --> 00:09:39,620
Well, between me and you?

241
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:40,955
Yeah.

242
00:09:40,955 --> 00:09:42,249
In this day and age

243
00:09:42,249 --> 00:09:44,543
how dumb do you have to be
to get pregnant?

244
00:09:44,543 --> 00:09:46,920
Hey, you know,
sometimes you can
do everything right.

245
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:49,339
Everyone can wear
everything they're
supposed to wear

246
00:09:49,339 --> 00:09:51,966
and one of those little
guys just gets through.

247
00:09:51,966 --> 00:09:53,552
How?

248
00:09:53,552 --> 00:09:56,846
I don't know.
Maybe they have tools.

249
00:09:56,846 --> 00:09:58,390
Well, I-I talked to her

250
00:09:58,390 --> 00:10:01,017
and, uh, she's definitely
going to have this baby.

251
00:10:01,017 --> 00:10:04,062
You know, she said she's going
to raise it on her own.

252
00:10:04,062 --> 00:10:06,481
Well, maybe that's...
maybe that's really brave.

253
00:10:06,481 --> 00:10:08,024
Maybe.

254
00:10:08,024 --> 00:10:10,485
I just hope she realizes
how hard it's going to be.

255
00:10:12,446 --> 00:10:14,030
Maybe she hasn't really

256
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:16,032
thought it through
that much.

257
00:10:17,451 --> 00:10:19,369
Well, there's a lot
to think about.

258
00:10:19,369 --> 00:10:20,703
I mean, how is she...

259
00:10:20,703 --> 00:10:22,747
how is she going
to handle this financially?

260
00:10:22,747 --> 00:10:24,832
How is she going
to juggle work? How...?

261
00:10:24,832 --> 00:10:26,501
Does she realize
she's not going

262
00:10:26,501 --> 00:10:29,170
to have a date again
for the next, like, 18 years?

263
00:10:32,257 --> 00:10:33,716
I don't know.

264
00:10:36,636 --> 00:10:38,305
Are you okay?

265
00:10:38,305 --> 00:10:40,140
Mm-hmm.

266
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:41,682
I'm just thinking
